Stage B. The demand of a skill, by intervention on the data generator
   By its formula an output of skill m depends on the input only through 4 numbers, the projections of z on U_sub[m],
   and the skill's own gate. That is 5 directions. The other 4 gates and the 3 nuisance inputs have no effect.
   Here each of the 24 inputs is moved in turn, up and down by 1e-6, and the generator is run again.
   skill 0: Jacobian rank at 200 inputs: least 5, most 5; median singular values over the largest: 1.000, 0.786, 0.600, 0.319, 0.033, 0.000, 0.000, 0.000
            largest effect of the 7 unused inputs: 0.0e+00
   skill 1: Jacobian rank at 200 inputs: least 5, most 5; median singular values over the largest: 1.000, 0.735, 0.493, 0.223, 0.024, 0.000, 0.000, 0.000
            largest effect of the 7 unused inputs: 0.0e+00

